       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\n- **Requested:** ibuprofen 1600 mg PO four times daily, which is 6,400 mg/day.\n- **Usual limits:** a single dose is generally capped at 800 mg. The maximum daily dose for adults is 3,200 mg/day under physician supervision, and 1,200 mg/day for OTC use.\n- **Risk:** this order is twice the maximum daily dose. It raises the risk of GI bleeding, acute kidney injury, and cardiovascular events, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **800 mg PO four times daily:** 3,200 mg/day, the usual maximum.\n- **400\u2013600 mg PO every 6 hours:** a common regimen for pain or inflammation.\n- **1600 mg total per day:** for example, 400 mg four times daily.\n\nIf you really want the 1600 mg dose four times daily, tell me and add a note explaining the clinical reason. I can enter it with that note, though pharmacy will probably flag it. Otherwise, tell me the corrected dose and I'll enter it right away."
